// Test: bugfixes/ef89_method_call_on_local_field_access
// Grammar: three_level_method_call vs. method_call on property_access (§method_chains)
// Semantic: CODEGEN-METHOD-CALL-ON-PLUGIN-EMITTED-BODY-CONCRETE-FIELD-ACCESS
//   (fingerprint ef89ed7c4daa, 0.33.108). Pest grammar rule
//   `three_level_method_call = identifier "." identifier "." method_name "(" ...`
//   at src/parser/grammar.pest:314 eagerly matches `entity.id.toString()`
//   as a namespace-class-method call (the shape intended for
//   `compare.integer.greaterThan(a, b)`) because the parser has no scope
//   information to distinguish a local variable from a namespace. The
//   resolver then routed it as a StaticMethodCall which the codegen
//   couldn't resolve to a real function, producing
//   `Function 'entity.id.toString' not found in function map`.
//
// The bug was reported against the frame.data v3.0.12 plugin path where
//   `_emit_stmt_from_source` on `"[" + entity.id.toString() + "]"` (in
//   Widget.delete's body) tripped the wrong pest rule. Hand-written source
//   of the same expression compiled cleanly because the surrounding
//   statements led pest to a different alternative — but that was luck,
//   not a real fix.
//
// Fix (0.33.111+): src/resolver/resolver_impl.rs::resolve_static_method_call_expression
//   now looks up `namespace[0]` in the symbol table before trusting the
//   parser's static-call classification. If the first segment binds to a
//   local variable or parameter (SymbolKind::Variable / Parameter), the
//   whole call is rewritten as
//     MethodCall(FieldAccess(local, field_name), method, args)
//   and resolution recurses. Legitimate namespace calls
//   (`compare.integer.greaterThan(a, b)`) are unaffected because `compare`
//   doesn't resolve to a local variable.
//
// This pin exercises the exact shape from the plugin-emitted delete body:
//   an instance-method call chained off a field access on a local
//   variable, embedded in a string concat. If the resolver ever regresses
//   to trusting three_level_method_call blindly, the compile fails with
//   "Function 'w.id.toString' not found in function map".
//
// Fixed in: compiler 0.33.111
//
// Expected output:
//   [42]

start:
	Widget w = Widget()
	string params = "[" + w.id.toString() + "]"
	print(params)

class Widget
	public:
		integer id
	constructor()
		id = 42
